  "html": "<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"Amen Slicer — running on the Game Boy&#x27;s 4-shade LCD\" class=\"\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/amen-slicer/gameboy.png\" alt=\"Amen Slicer — running on the Game Boy&#x27;s 4-shade LCD\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/projects/amen-slicer/gameboy.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/projects/amen-slicer/gameboy.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/amen-slicer/gameboy.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/projects/amen-slicer/gameboy.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"Amen Slicer — running on the Game Boy&#x27;s 4-shade LCD\" width=\"1842\" height=\"1728\" style=\"--splay-rot:-0.6deg;\" data-dimensions=\"1842×1728\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm img-splay aspect-square w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"><figcaption class=\"\">Amen Slicer — running on the Game Boy's 4-shade LCD</figcaption></figure>\nA breakbeat slicer / performance instrument for the Game Boy Advance — 13 amen flavors, sync-locked clock, live stutters/FX/crush, and a reactive generative visualizer. Butano/C++.<p class=\"\"></p>\n<p class=\"\">I am SO stoked about this one. This is basically because I am getting my music table set up again — I have a Maschine+ and an FM synthesizer, and I just need a device that makes it easy to drop in, beat sync, and chop up amen breaks in time with the other music hardware.</p>\n<p class=\"\">I made one for the Game Boy (Miyoo Mini, really) to experiment with making my own Game Boy game utilities — or really, shaping/forming the Miyoo Mini into my own dream piece of hacker music gear.</p>\n<p class=\"\">Plug in the Game Boy — the headphone port is a little janky but you can get it — then sync up the 1 from the Game Boy, pick a sample, chop it around while the other instruments happen.</p>\n<p class=\"\">I also made a Rust macOS amen slice breaker app that works with the 64-pad grid controller over MIDI — <a href=\"https://github.com/ejfox/amen-grid\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"external-link group inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400\" data-preview-url=\"https://github.com/ejfox/amen-grid\">amen-grid<svg class=\"inline-block w-4 h-4 ml-1 opacity-50 dark:opacity-75 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity align-text-bottom\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1em\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12c0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385c.6.113.82-.258.82-.577c0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04c-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729c1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236c1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998c.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605c-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93c0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22c-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176c0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23c.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405c1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405c2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23c.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176c.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22c0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92c.42.36.81 1.096.81 2.22c0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286c0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12\" class=\"\"></path></svg></a>.</p>",
